{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1b788bb8769aea9d2754e96ad71ed0be1586b78","commits":["cd184fe0e9f2f1d171538282ef98c4b9d28ea304","d5148b29a9903ff622ccdac6b3f8e41714d118c5","a473274148f324844ef946b711cb8b52647d1faa","726e1c765e4bd9f5fead531662da9b7f8f0b8950","a9b09551ecc2b4a51440cd9ba4de33f92fcb4580","b44da7e4f326c2c00985e47e8f7e28817bc3d308","62eb3bcb67705fd037223176198e1d4820812615","dee8d8a7020ea72857218f5c556d3db17c2f4361","7c83786a6bf378de61076b43de92f3babfe8f384"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Custom exception hierarchy replaces ValueError.** rlsbl now raises ConfigError, WorkspaceError, ChangelogError, VersionError, and ReleaseFileError instead of bare ValueError. Code that catches ValueError from rlsbl APIs must update to catch the new types.","type":"breaking"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1b9b5bb204075e4c6c84b399124e07347866833","commits":["b41bcf95da5f8dcc2a3b89f40ebbbcfc094e388f"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Ultranorm variant cap is now a hard error.** check-name with highly-ambiguous names now errors instead of silently warning and continuing with incomplete results.","type":"breaking"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1ba6947de50b23037ca4242aec62daea5691427","commits":["c0bcc74ea8be6cfb74a7e99f621874d21779ed38"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**npm CI templates handle missing lockfiles.** Templates now use npm ci when a lockfile exists and fall back to npm install when absent. Zero-dependency wrapper packages are auto-detected and skip CI generation.","type":"feature"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1bafa00051a8fb1595f4f4f81c152b9b24cae6a","commits":["725d129acaa68ce23555b7c606bc41f0be3078c5"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**npm wrapper improvements.** bin/cli.js now verifies Python >= 3.11, checks rlsbl is installed (with clear error messages), and supports Windows via python3/python/py fallback.","type":"feature"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1bb84f7150b5fbf1d0743b9a07316f91dd741ca","commits":["a7ec239595a91def8caefba87e8c50f47926d62c"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Deploy: local_steps field.** Deploy targets can now run local commands (cross-compilation, file transfers) before SSH-based remote steps.","type":"feature"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1bc0521518b1c00de91408e89091c916a0edf13","commits":["6acf645005c72c87531db5039524d886e7c0c208"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**target-count selfdoc directive.** New directive dynamically generates the release target count with a link to the targets documentation page.","type":"feature"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1bdfba8d74b5a70394c4f3aa0da47ece6bac10d","commits":["b1cb80de25e6cb2b2f7f6c177cadcd8b7a89512d"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Remove silent data truncation.** Changelog commit messages and batch exclusion reasons are no longer silently truncated at 72/60 characters.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c0277c8425029d8b6640cdb6dfe7aea3fca4aa","commits":["97d4f4db19facbfc7a080e56f338c7ef02093591","5c1220df4e293cde1e0737e9f7bda882931854df","e9492de961d9139921d8e467eab4272d09d0b7ab","d08fa37da01d9dae4958590ad94a072fc324ed77","6671ad578700e1f68d24c7079cb76a73f49780c7"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Remove display truncation caps.** Unreleased subjects, pre-push missing commits, OTA native files, orphan hashes, and discover descriptions now show full content instead of capping at arbitrary limits.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c1a57a64117101de2140fa892838b587b115c0","commits":["034b1740093e51522b74d7db17f0c7170b0f3bd3"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Changelog regeneration preserves release metadata.** Descriptions and context from archived release .toml files are now read during CHANGELOG.md regeneration, fixing data loss on subsequent regenerations.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c2cef01d6bbffa572b4b0bb27aca17c7ed66cb","commits":["62b6ef7c4366dfc1b9becd4d86ea9d5b076d0794"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**deps-unused no longer flags guarded imports.** Imports inside try/except ImportError blocks now count as used, fixing false positives for optional dependencies.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c5e4523969859e8abc42cba3e411b7870e8539","commits":["4254af2ea3fef62e36fbc74ae49a87c12bba2dc8"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Test context detection uses root-relative matching.** src/test/ is no longer falsely classified as test code. Added testdata/ and integration_test/ patterns.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c6b249d5b659b42311449ca9c547a25680424b","commits":["389e2744fc91170f3346e58686ccf4c04744550e"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**BFS and topological sort use correct data structures.** Workspace graph BFS uses deque (O(1) dequeue) and topological sort uses heapq instead of re-sorting.","type":"fix"}
{"format_version":2,"id":"18dc8810f1c75dcf45cbd19182e34e009bccff3392586bc5","commits":["7bc3a18e61dd16edfeb27e9284f5310211f04873"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Spec docs corrected.** Fixed incorrect claim that spec target has no ci_templates.","type":"fix"}
